exity per line of code.\n# Usefulness: Indicates whether a module\'s complexity scales linearly or non-linearly with its size. Modules with disproportionately high complexity per line are more likely to have defects.\ndf[\'cyclomatic_complexity_per_loc\'] = df[\'v(g)\'] / (df[\'loc\'] + 1e-5)\n\n# design_complexity_per_loc\n# Ratio of design complexity (iv(g)) to lines of code (loc). Measures design complexity per line.\n# Usefulness: High design complexity compared to module size could indicate areas prone to errors or rigid code.\ndf[\'design_complexity_per_loc\'] = df[\'iv(g)\'] / (df[\'loc\'] + 1e-5)\n```end\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Apply Log Transformation to Highly Skewed Features**\n#### Code:\n```python\n# log_effort\n# Log transformation of Halstead \'effort\' (e). Reduces the extreme skewness of the `e` distribution.\n# Usefulness: Captures diminishing returns in development effort as effort increases due to common developer constraints or bottlenecks.\ndf[\'log_effort\'] = df[\'e\'].apply(lambda x: np.log1p(x))\n\n# log_volume\n# Log transformation of Halstead \'volume\' (v). Reduces the extreme skewness of `v` distribution.\n# Usefulness: Represents the cognitive load in a scaled way, where small increases in volume have a larger effect at lower values than at higher volumes.\ndf[\'log_volume\'] = df[\'v\'].apply(lambda x: np.log1p(x))\n```end\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Engineer "Code Clarity Ratio"**\n#### Code:\n```python\n# code_to_comment_ratio\n# Ratio of lines of code (lOCode) to lines of comments (lOComment). Adds 1 to the denominator to avoid division by zero.\n# Usefulness: Indicates the documentation quality of the code. Modules with no or poor comments are more difficult to maintain, which may lead to defects.\ndf[\'code_to_comment_ratio\'] = df[\'lOCode\'] / (df[\'lOComment\'] + 1)\n\n# blank_to_total_lines_ratio\n# Ratio of blank lines (lOBlank) to total lines (loc). Measures how "spaced out" the code is.\n# Usefulness: Helps assess code readability and adherence to spacing conventions, which may correlate with defect-prone modules.\ndf[\'blank_to_total_lines_ratio\'] = df[\'lOBlank\'] / (df[\'loc\'] + 1)\n```end\n\n---\n\n### Evaluation for Dropping Columns\n\nHighly skewed and redundant features should be considered for removal after feature engineering and modeling. For instance:\n\n```python\n# Dropping feature \'locCodeAndComment\'\n# Explanation: \'locCodeAndComment\' has an extremely small variance and is mostly zero across the dataset, making it uninformative.\ndf.drop(columns=[\'locCodeAndComment\'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\nBy focusing on interactions, transformations, and ratios across complexity, size, documentation, and readability dimensions, the above process aims to improve the downstream task\'s predictive signal on software defect likelihood.']
