# Feature description: Ratio of v(g) (cyclomatic complexity) to the number of lines of code (loc). 
df['cyclomatic_density'] = df['v(g)'] / (df['loc'] + 1e-6)  # Adding a small denominator to avoid division by zero
# Usefulness: This provides insights about how dense the complexity is within the context of the code's size. Modules with high cyclomatic complexity relative to lines of code are more prone to defects as they might involve overly complex logic in a small area.

# 2. Feature name: adjusted_operator_operand_ratio
# Feature description: operator_operand_ratio adjusted with logarithmic scaling to reduce the impact of extreme outliers.
df['adjusted_operator_operand_ratio'] = np.log1p(df['operator_operand_ratio'])
# Usefulness: The original range of operator_operand_ratio from near 0 to very high values can distort model training. A log transformation reduces skewness and helps the model focus on more meaningful variation across modules.

# 3. Feature name: control_density
# Feature description: Ratio of branchCount to the number of lines of code (loc) or the density of control structures in the code.
df['control_density'] = df['branchCount'] / (df['loc'] + 1e-6)
# Usefulness: Modules with a high density of control structures relative to their size can indicate complexity hotspots. This feature could help highlight modules that are more error-prone due to overly intertwined control flow logic.
end

